// shader-differential float mode (`@rt f32`) — the k program.
//
// Paints uniform k on every pixel.  The guest sets k from RAW binary32
// words (manifest ka=/kb=, the init sentinel, the canary), so this one
// container is the init draw before every row, the control-f32-k rows
// (words, ulp, sub8, nan) and control-f32-frames: each asserts that the
// exact words come back, which is what qualifies the float readback.
void main(uniform float4 k, out float4 color : COLOR)
{
    color = k;
}
